Its source headers allow GPL version 3 or later; see its LICENSE and source
headers. That license is not overridden by the repository's GPL-3.0-only notice.
The new Mac adapter implements its public TTF1 wire protocol independently;
the GPL firmware implementation is not linked into the macOS executable.
scripts/tests/ducker_contract.c compiles upstream's test harness by inclusion
for testing only, with the upstream copyright and licensing retained.

DuckerCompatibility is an optional BT Paste overlay for the pinned Ducker
source. It isolates the SDK serial profile from the firmware's automatic RPC
registration without changing its GAP security configuration. The build script
retains the original Bluetooth implementation as upstream_bt.inc and packages
the complete modified source alongside the resulting FAP. This is a development
variant, not an upstream release. See DuckerCompatibility/BUILD.md.
